            <ArticleTitle>[Symptomatic triangular bone. A case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>494-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Os triangulare is an accessory bone found in the triangular cartilage of the wrist just distal to the end of the ulna and is generally asymptomatic. A case report of symptomatic Os triangulare is reported. Treatment associated immobilization and anti-inflammatory medication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
